{"execution_score":5,"aesthetic_score":5,"feedback":"The 3×3 grid of Lucy statues is a literal interpretation of Kusama's repetition but misses the obsessive, overwhelming quality — nine copies in a neat grid reads as a layout exercise, not infinity made visible. The polka-dot concept only shows up as round point sprites, not as actual dots patterning the surface; true Kusama would have spherical dots growing on or erupting from the mesh skin. The red/white/yellow palette is on-theme but the additive blending washes it into hot pink noise at overlap zones, losing the crisp dot-on-field contrast that defines her work. A stronger version would tile dozens of smaller Lucys in a logarithmic spiral or mirror-room recursion, apply actual surface-mapped polka dots via a dot-product threshold in the fragment shader, and use a restrained red-on-white or yellow-on-black field rather than additive glow."}
```

