{"execution_score":7,"aesthetic_score":7,"feedback":"The Kusama polka-dot concept lands clearly — red dots on ivory Lucy with concentric repetition and a dotted floor sell the infinity-room obsession. The central figure is well-framed and readable, and the ring layout gives genuine depth. To push it further: the outer ring copies are too small and sparse to read as anything but noise at distance — either increase their particle count or fade them into a fog/mirror boundary. The breathing pulse is nearly invisible; lean into the obsessive repetition more by having dot frequency or size oscillate per-copy with slight phase offsets, so the field feels alive rather than static. A subtle reflection or mirrored duplicate below the floor plane would strengthen the infinity-room reference considerably."}
